    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410-a1">

                <pb facs="0458" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg424"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 849. Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 21.</p>
                <p>In case of expropriation on account of the opening of the Interoceanic Canal and
                    in consideration of the expenses which the company shall have defrayed, the
                    company shall be indemnified for the material value of the undertaking by said
                    (canal) company, which company shall have to pay the indemnity, it being
                    understood that the Government of Nicaragua will in no case be obliged to pay
                    (the Atlas Company) any indemnity.</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 22.</p>
                <p>In no case nor on any account will the company or its representative have the
                    right to ask diplomatic interference. The home of the company shall remain in
                    Nicaragua.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
